                    insight_fundable:       `Fundable venture: you matched the idea to the runway, validated willingness-to-pay cheaply, read the evidence honestly and earned the R$25M round on validated learning — not on a demo or the sponsor's word. This cohort breaks the “kill it late” pattern.`,
                    insight_validated:      `Credible validated learning: traction cleared the paid-pilot bar and your evidence is real. Tighten the unit-economics case and the R$25M gate is within reach.`,
                    insight_kill:           `A disciplined kill: the evidence didn't clear the bar, and you returned capital before the runway was gone. That preserves credibility and keeps Bandeira Labs alive — a timely no-go is a success of the gate, not a failure.`,
                    insight_vanity:         `Vanity trajectory: sign-ups and demo praise flattered the venture, but paid-pilot conversion never cleared 35%. This is exactly the optimism that burned R$14M before.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the paid-pilot bar. Re-examine where the runway went — most likely an idea that outran the runway, a build before validation, or a metric that measured applause instead of money.`,
                    insight_built:          `You built the real platform before validating, spending ~R$4,2M and four months. Half the runway went to build, not learning — the precise mistake the new gate exists to stop.`,
                    insight_burned:         `The runway hit empty: with nothing left to pivot or scale with, even real learning couldn't be acted on. Runway = cash ÷ burn, and you burned it building rather than learning.`,
                    insight_sunk:           `Sunk cost drove a decision it should never have touched. The money already spent is gone either way; the call belongs to the remaining runway and the evidence.`,
                    insight_rotasmart:      `RotaSmart's enterprise sales cycle (9–12 months) always outran your 9-month runway. The biggest market is worthless if you can't reach validation before the cash runs out.`,
                    insight_sponsor:        `You rode the sponsor's verbal interest rather than testing it. One client's “maybe” is not a signed pilot — the discipline is to falsify it cheaply before you scale.`,
                    insight_strongtraction: `Strong, real traction: learning and paid-pilot conversion moved together with runway still in hand. That is a venture the committee can fund with confidence.`,

                    hint_runway:            `Your runway is almost gone with rounds still to play — there may be nothing left to act on your evidence. Protect remaining cash and avoid any further build.`,
                    hint_built:             `You've sunk the runway into a full build before validating. Shift the remaining cash to cheap willingness-to-pay tests before the gate, or you'll reach it with a guess.`,
                    hint_vanity:            `You're leaning on vanity metrics. Sign-ups and demos don't clear the gate — paid-pilot conversion and retention do. Redefine evidence around money committed.`,
